      "id": 158968,
      "name": "Alex",
      "username": "Alex",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/alex/{size}/2059_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-10T06:48:13.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I sort of assumed there had&nbsp;<em>always</em> been multiple timelines, and the \"shattering\" was referring to snarls and paradoxes that formed when so many heroes and villains started messing with it, hence the Time Cataclysm environment. But now that we know the end of the card game marks the end of the multiverse as we know it... hmm. Do alternate planes of existence, like the Realm of Dischord, count as additional universes in the multiverse, or is the multiverse simply the sum total of every variant timeline? Or is the Realm of Dischord an alternate timeline, too, just one where things developed differently way, WAY earlier in the multiverse's formation, such that it bears no resemblence to our world?</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:39:10.460Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
