      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chaosmancer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/48/1977_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chaosmancer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think we've linked it heavily to OblivAeon creating his singularity to destroy everything.&nbsp;I remember hearing that Visionary did not create the shattering, merely used the cracks caused by it to time travel. MY Forum-foo is too weak to find where that was said though</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think the opening story in the KS makes it sound pretty clear that OblivAeon itself was the source of the shattering timelines. In order to achieve his goal of condencing all of the multiverse down into a single whole to destroy it, creating those cracks in time was a key first step it seems.</p>\n<p>Did anyone have a different reading of it?</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:39:10.669Z",
